    SW_INT_STAT  0:0  ALPHA {"This is a software initiated interrupt (SWI).  If software writes in this register bit, SOFT_INITIATED_INT_STAT would take on '1'.  Software would poll GPIOPAD_INT_STAT to determine whether this SWI occurred.  To clear this software initiated interrupt, software should write to SOFT_INITIATED_INT_STAT_AK, which is a bit located in the GPIOPAD_INT_STAT_AK register, and SW_INITIATED_INT_STAT will return to '0'. " = 0x0 }  ;
