CB_PERFCOUNTER0_SELECT   <GpuF0Reg:0x37004> <GpuF0VF0Reg:0x37004> <GpuF0VF1Reg:0x37004> <GpuF0VF2Reg:0x37004> <GpuF0VF3Reg:0x37004> <GpuF0VF4Reg:0x37004> <GpuF0VF5Reg:0x37004> <GpuF0VF6Reg:0x37004> <GpuF0VF7Reg:0x37004> <GpuF0VF8Reg:0x37004> <GpuF0VF9Reg:0x37004> <GpuF0VF10Reg:0x37004> <GpuF0VF11Reg:0x37004> <GpuF0VF12Reg:0x37004> <GpuF0VF13Reg:0x37004> <GpuF0VF14Reg:0x37004> <GpuF0VF15Reg:0x37004> <GpuF1Reg:0x37004>   32    {
    PERF_SEL  8:0  ALPHA {"CB_PERF_SEL_NONE: Count nothing " = 0x0, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_BUSY: Number of busy cycles " = 0x1, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CORE_SCLK_VLD: Number of cycles that the core clock is enabled. " = 0x2, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_REG_SCLK0_VLD: Number of cycles that the register clock is enabled. (Non-harvestable) " = 0x3, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_REG_SCLK1_VLD: Number of cycles that the register clock is enabled. (harvestable) " = 0x4, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_DRAWN_QUAD: This is the number of drawn quads.
Use CB_PERF_SEL_DRAWN_BUSY as denominator to get per clock rates.
  Filtering using CB_PERFCOUNTER_FILTER fields has an effect in this mode.  " = 0x5, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_DRAWN_PIXEL: This is the number of drawn pixels.
Use CB_PERF_SEL_DRAWN_BUSY as denominator to get per clock rates.
Filtering using CB_PERFCOUNTER_FILTER fields has an effect in this mode. " = 0x6, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_DRAWN_QUAD_FRAGMENT: This is the number of drawn quad fragments.
Use CB_PERF_SEL_DRAWN_BUSY as denominator to get per clock rates.
  Filtering using CB_PERFCOUNTER_FILTER fields has an effect in this mode.  " = 0x7, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_DRAWN_TILE: This is the number of drawn tiles.
Use CB_PERF_SEL_DRAWN_BUSY as denominator to get per clock rates.
Filtering using CB_PERFCOUNTER_FILTER fields has an effect in this mode.
 This counter is slightly broken in that it actually counts the number of tiles reaching fragop.  Some of these tiles may be empty when there is fast clear or compression. " = 0x8, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_TILE_VALID_READY: Number of cycles the DB to CB tile interface is valid and ready.  This is measured after the input fifo. It counts tiles + events. Subtract CB_PERF_SEL_EVENT to get the count of tiles " = 0x9, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_TILE_VALID_READYB: Number of cycles the DB to CB tile interface is valid and not ready.  This is measured after the input fifo. " = 0xa, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_TILE_VALIDB_READY: Number of cycles the DB to CB tile interface is not valid and ready.  This is measured after the input fifo. " = 0xb, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_TILE_VALIDB_READYB: Number of cycles the DB to CB tile interface is not valid and not ready.  This is measured after the input fifo. " = 0xc, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_FC_TILE_VALID_READY: Number of cycles the cmask to fmask tile interface is valid and ready. This interface counts tile times enabled render targets plus events. This will be different from CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_TILE_VALID_READY because each tile is replicated by the number of enabled render targets (events are not) " = 0xd, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_FC_TILE_VALID_READYB: Number of cycles the cmask to fmask tile interface is valid and not ready " = 0xe, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_FC_TILE_VALIDB_READY: Number of cycles the cmask to fmask tile interface is not valid and ready " = 0xf, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_FC_TILE_VALIDB_READYB: Number of cycles the cmask to fmask tile interface is not valid and not ready " = 0x10, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_MERGE_TILE_ONLY_VALID_READY: Number of cycles the Merge tile interface has a valid tile-only tile and is ready.  Measured at tile input to merge. " = 0x11, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_MERGE_TILE_ONLY_VALID_READYB: Number of cycles the Merge tile interface has a valid tile-only tile and is not ready.  Measured at tile input to merge. " = 0x12, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_LQUAD_VALID_READY: Number of cycles the DB to CB lquad interface is valid and ready.  This is measured after the input fifo. This is counting lquad which for fast modes are the same as quads but for slow mode are twice the number of quads. To get the number of quads on this interface use: CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_LQUAD_VALID_READY - CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_32_ABGR/2 " = 0x13, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_LQUAD_VALID_READYB: Number of cycles the DB to CB lquad interface is valid and not ready.  This is measured after the input fifo " = 0x14, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_LQUAD_VALIDB_READY: Number of cycles the DB to CB lquad interface is not valid and ready.  This is measured after the input fifo " = 0x15, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_LQUAD_VALIDB_READYB: Number of cycles the DB to CB lquad interface is not valid and not ready.  This is measured after the input fifo " = 0x16, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_NO_TILE: Number of cycles that a quad has arrived over the lquad interface but the corresponding tile has not arrived yet. " = 0x17, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_32_R: Number of transactions/quads on the DB_CB_lquad interface that use the EXPORT_32_R (FAST MODE) format. Sum of all CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_* should match CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_LQUAD_VALID_READY " = 0x18, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_32_AR: Number of transactions/quads on the DB_CB_lquad interface that use the EXPORT_32_AR (FAST MODE) format. Sum of all CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_* should match CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_LQUAD_VALID_READY " = 0x19, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_32_GR: Number of transactions/quads on the DB_CB_lquad interface that use the EXPORT_32_GR (FAST MODE) format. Sum of all CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_* should match CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_LQUAD_VALID_READY " = 0x1a, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_32_ABGR: Number of transactions on the DB_CB_lquad interface that use the EXPORT_32_ABGR (SLOW MODE) format. To get the number of quads divide this number by 2. Sum of all CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_* should match CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_LQUAD_VALID_READY " = 0x1b, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_FP16_ABGR: Number of transactions/quads on the DB_CB_lquad interface that use the EXPORT_FP16_ABGR (FAST MODE) format. Sum of all CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_* should match CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_LQUAD_VALID_READY " = 0x1c, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_SIGNED16_ABGR: Number of transactions/quads on the DB_CB_lquad interface that use the EXPORT_SIGNED16_ABGR (FAST MODE) format. Sum of all CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_* should match CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_LQUAD_VALID_READY " = 0x1d, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_UNSIGNED16_ABGR: Number of transactions/quads on the DB_CB_lquad interface that use the EXPORT_UNSIGNED16_ABGR (FAST MODE) format. Sum of all CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_* should match CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_LQUAD_VALID_READY " = 0x1e, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_KILLED_BY_EXTRA_PIXEL_EXPORT: Number of quads that were killed because they were an extra pixel export from the shader based on CB_TARGET_MASK, CB_SHADER_MASK settings. " = 0x1f, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_KILLED_BY_COLOR_INVALID: Number of quads that was killed because their render target had CB_COLOR_INFO.FORMAT set to invalid. " = 0x20, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_KILLED_BY_NULL_TARGET_SHADER_MASK: Number of quads that were killed because of null (target&shader) mask. " = 0x21, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_KILLED_BY_NULL_SAMPLE_MASK: Number of quads that were killed because of a null sample mask. " = 0x22, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_KILLED_BY_DISCARD_PIXEL: Number of quads that were killed because they were blending but enabled optimization to discard all the pixels of the quad. This optimization can be disabled by setting DISABLE_BLEND_OPT_DISCARD_PIXEL. " = 0x23, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CLEAR_QUAD_VALID_READY: Number of cycles in the fmask logic that the read_latency fifo to the clear interface is valid and ready. This is counting quads + events. The number of quads should match the number of quads on the lquad interface (i.e. CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_LQUAD_VALID_READY - CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_32_ABGR/2) minus any quads that are dropped and show up in the perf counters CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_KILLED_BY_* " = 0x24, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CLEAR_QUAD_VALID_READYB: Number of cycles in the fmask logic that the read_latency fifo to the clear interface is valid and not ready. " = 0x25, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CLEAR_QUAD_VALIDB_READY: Number of cycles in the fmask logic that the read_latency fifo to the clear interface is not valid and ready. " = 0x26, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CLEAR_QUAD_VALIDB_READYB: Number of cycles in the fmask logic that the read_latency fifo to the clear interface is not valid and not ready. " = 0x27, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FOP_IN_VALID_READY: Number of cycles the fragop unit input interface is valid and ready. This is counting quads + events. The number of quads here should match CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CLEAR_QUAD_VALID_READY plus any quads inserted by the fast_clear_eliminate (fc_clear) block " = 0x28, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FOP_IN_VALID_READYB: Number of cycles the fragop unit input interface is valid and not ready " = 0x29, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FOP_IN_VALIDB_READY: Number of cycles the fragop unit input interface is not valid and ready " = 0x2a, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FOP_IN_VALIDB_READYB: Number of cycles the fragop unit input interface is not valid and not ready " = 0x2b, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CC_QUADFRAG_VALID_READY: Number of cycles the fmask to color cache interface is valid and ready. This is counting quad fragments + events. The number of quads here should match CB_PERF_SEL_FOP_IN_VALID_READY times the number of fragments created for each of these quads by the fragop block " = 0x2c, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CC_QUADFRAG_VALID_READYB: Number of cycles the fmask to color cache interface is valid and not ready " = 0x2d, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CC_QUADFRAG_VALIDB_READY: Number of cycles the fmask to color cache interface is not valid and ready " = 0x2e, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CC_QUADFRAG_VALIDB_READYB: Number of cycles the fmask to color cache interface is not valid and not ready " = 0x2f, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_IB_SR_FRAG_VALID_READY: Number of cycles the color cache input block's serializer interface is valid and ready. This is counting quad fragments + events. The number of quads here should match CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CC_QUADFRAG_VALID_READY times the number of cycles needed to handle these quads due to any HW limitations like 32bit floating point blending, linear or linear_aligned array mode etc " = 0x30, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_IB_SR_FRAG_VALID_READYB: Number of cycles the color cache input block's serializer two-lookup interface is valid and not ready " = 0x31, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_IB_SR_FRAG_VALIDB_READY: Number of cycles the color cache input block's serializer two-lookup interface is not valid and ready " = 0x32, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_IB_SR_FRAG_VALIDB_READYB: Number of cycles the color cache input block's serializer to two-lookup interface is not valid and not ready " = 0x33, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_IB_TB_FRAG_VALID_READY: Number of cycles the color cache input block to tag block interface is valid and ready. This is counting quad fragments + events. The number of quads here should match CB_PERF_SEL_CC_IB_SR_FRAG_VALID_READY + CB_PERF_SEL_TWO_PROBE_QUAD_FRAGMENT. " = 0x34, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_IB_TB_FRAG_VALID_READYB: Number of cycles the color cache input block to tag block interface is valid and not ready " = 0x35, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_IB_TB_FRAG_VALIDB_READY: Number of cycles the color cache input block to tag block interface is not valid and ready " = 0x36, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_IB_TB_FRAG_VALIDB_READYB: Number of cycles the color cache input block to tag block interface is not valid and not ready " = 0x37, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_BC_EVENFRAG_VALID_READY: Number of cycles the reorder_buffer to blend_control interface (evenfrag) is valid and ready. This is counting quad fragments + events. The number of quads in (CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_BC_EVENFRAG_VALID_READY + CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_BC_ODDFRAG_VALID_READY) equals quads in CB_PERF_SEL_CC_IB_SR_FRAG_VALID_READY as the de-serializer collapses the two cache probe quads back into one. The quads are split into two fifos, evenfifo stores the quads with even 32B address. Events go down both paths " = 0x38, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_BC_EVENFRAG_VALID_READYB: Number of cycles the reorder_buffer to blend_control interface (evenfrag) is valid and not ready " = 0x39, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_BC_EVENFRAG_VALIDB_READY: Number of cycles the reorder_buffer to blend_control interface (evenfrag) is not valid and ready " = 0x3a, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_BC_EVENFRAG_VALIDB_READYB: Number of cycles the reorder_buffer to blend_control interface (evenfrag) is not valid and not ready " = 0x3b, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_BC_ODDFRAG_VALID_READY: Number of cycles the reorder_buffer to blend_control interface (oddfrag) is valid and ready. This is counting quad fragments + events. The number of quads in (CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_BC_EVENFRAG_VALID_READY + CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_BC_ODDFRAG_VALID_READY) equals quads in CB_PERF_SEL_CC_IB_SR_FRAG_VALID_READY as the de-serializer collapses the two cache probe quads back into one. The quads are split into two fifos, oddfifo stores the quads with odd 32B address. Events go down both paths " = 0x3c, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_BC_ODDFRAG_VALID_READYB: Number of cycles the reorder_buffer to blend_control interface (oddfrag) is valid and not ready " = 0x3d, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_BC_ODDFRAG_VALIDB_READY: Number of cycles the reorder_buffer to blend_control interface (oddfrag) is not valid and ready " = 0x3e, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_BC_ODDFRAG_VALIDB_READYB: Number of cycles the reorder_buffer to blend_control interface (oddfrag) is not valid and not ready " = 0x3f, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_BC_CS_FRAG_VALID: Number of cycles the blend_control to cache_storage interface is valid. This is counting quad fragments + events. The number of quads here should match CB_PERF_SEL_CC_IB_SR_FRAG_VALID_READY " = 0x40, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_HIT: Number of tile transactions that hit cmask cache (TAG HIT && SECTOR HIT). It is a hit if you hit the tag and a sector in that tag meaning that sector's data is valid.
Total probe transactions = incoming tile transactions (in compressed AA mode or single sample with fast clear mode) times render targets = CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_HIT+CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS. " = 0x41, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_TAG_MISS: Number of tile transactions that have cmask cache tag misses (TAG MISS).  A tag miss is when there isn't a tag that matches the input.  Because of sectoring, a tag hit does not imply that the required data is in the cache (i.e TAG HIT && SECTOR MISS). " = 0x42, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS: Number of tile transactions that have cmask cache sector miss (TAG MISS || SECTOR MISS).  A sector miss is when the required sector is not in the cache.  Tag misses are included in this count because a sector cannot be in the cache if there is no tag for it.
 Total transactions that have TAG HIT && SECTOR MISS = CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS - CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_TAG_MISS " = 0x43, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_REEVICTION_STALL: Number of cycles the cmask cache is stalled because it is trying to evict a line that already has a pending evict. This can happen when a cacheline has been written out to memory and waiting for the write ack gets a hit again, eventually becoming dirty and needing to be re-evicted. Since only one eviction per cacheline can be outstanding, the cache is stalled " = 0x44, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_EVICT_NONZERO_INFLIGHT_STALL: Number of cycles the cmask cache is stalled because it is trying to evict a line that has a nonzero inflight count.
When a cachelines LRU count reaches the scaled eviction point set by CM_CACHE_EVICT_POINT and it is still inflight then this counter get incremented
This is usually a sign that the cache is unable to withstand the memory read latency. CM_CACHE_EVICT_POINT can be set to a LOWER value to handle the increased read latency " = 0x45, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_REPLACE_PENDING_EVICT_STALL: Number of cycles the cmask cache is stalled because the line being replaced has a pending evict. This happens when the cacheline chosen for allocation on a miss is still waiting for its write-ack to return from a previous eviction. This is usually a sign that the cache is unable to withstand the memory write latency. CM_CACHE_EVICT_POINT can be set to a HIGHER value to handle the increased write latency " = 0x46, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_INFLIGHT_COUNTER_MAXIMUM_STALL: Number of cycles the cmask cache is stalled because one of the inflight counters has reached the maximum value. " = 0x47, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_READ_OUTPUT_STALL: Number of cycles the cmask cache is stalled because the read request output path is stalled. This can happen due to increased memory read request ask-go latency " = 0x48, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_WRITE_OUTPUT_STALL: Number of cycles the cmask cache is stalled because the write request output path is stalled. This can happen due to increased memory write request ask-go latency " = 0x49, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_ACK_OUTPUT_STALL: Number of cycles the cmask cache is stalled because the acknowledge output path is stalled. This can happen if the next stage in the pipeline (cmask cache read latency hiding fifo) is full and stalling the cmask cache so the cache cannot output any transactions. " = 0x4a, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_STALL: Number of cycles the cmask cache is stalled. This is the combined cache stall signal. " = 0x4b, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_FLUSH: This is the number of cmask cache flushes. " = 0x4c, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_TAGS_FLUSHED: Number of dirty tags that are flushed (the cmask cache has 32 tags). " = 0x4d, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_SECTORS_FLUSHED: Number of valid sectors (i.e they have valid data) per dirty tags that are flushed (the cmask cache has 1 sector per tag). The valid sectors may be dirty. The total valid non-dirty sectors in flushed out tags = CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_SECTORS_FLUSHED - CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_DIRTY_SECTORS_FLUSHED " = 0x4e, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_DIRTY_SECTORS_FLUSHED: Number of dirty sectors per dirty tags that are flushed (the cmask cache has 1 sector per tag). " = 0x4f, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_HIT: Number of tile transactions that hit the fmask cache  (TAG HIT && SECTOR HIT). It is a hit if you hit the tag and a sector in that tag meaning that sector's data is valid.
Total probe transactions = incoming tile transactions times render targets = CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_HIT+CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS. " = 0x50, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_TAG_MISS: Number of tile transactions that have fmask cache tag misses (TAG MISS).  A tag miss is when there isn't a tag that matches the input.  Because of sectoring, a tag hit does not imply that the required data is in the cache (i.e TAG HIT && SECTOR MISS). " = 0x51, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS: Number of tile transactions that have fmask cache sector miss (TAG MISS || SECTOR MISS).  A sector miss is when the required sector is not in the cache.  Tag misses are included in this count because a sector cannot be in the cache if there is no tag for it.
 Total transactions that have TAG HIT && SECTOR MISS = CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS - CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_TAG_MISS. " = 0x52, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_REEVICTION_STALL: Number of cycles the fmask cache is stalled because it is trying to evict a line that already has a pending evict. This can happen when a cacheline has been written out to memory and waiting for the write ack gets a hit again, eventually becoming dirty and needing to be re-evicted. Since only one eviction per cacheline can be outstanding, the cache is stalled. " = 0x53, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_EVICT_NONZERO_INFLIGHT_STALL: Number of cycles the fmask cache is stalled because it is trying to evict a line that has a nonzero inflight count.
When a cachelines LRU count reaches the scaled eviction point set by FC_CACHE_EVICT_POINT and it is still inflight then this counter get incremented
This is usually a sign that the cache is unable to withstand the memory read latency. FC_CACHE_EVICT_POINT can be set to a LOWER value to handle the increased read latency. " = 0x54, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_REPLACE_PENDING_EVICT_STALL: Number of cycles the fmask cache is stalled because the line being replaced has a pending evict. This happens when the cacheline chosen for allocation on a miss is still waiting for its write-ack to return from a previous eviction. This is usually a sign that the cache is unable to withstand the memory write latency. FC_CACHE_EVICT_POINT can be set to a HIGHER value to handle the increased write latency. " = 0x55, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_INFLIGHT_COUNTER_MAXIMUM_STALL: Number of cycles the fmask cache is stalled because one of the inflight counters has reached the maximum value. " = 0x56, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_READ_OUTPUT_STALL: Number of cycles the fmask cache is stalled because the read request output path is stalled. This can happen due to increased memory read request ask-go latency " = 0x57, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_WRITE_OUTPUT_STALL: Number of cycles the fmask cache is stalled because the write request output path is stalled.  This can happen due to increased memory write request ask-go latency " = 0x58, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_ACK_OUTPUT_STALL: Number of cycles the fmask cache is stalled because the acknowledge output path is stalled. This can happen if the next stage in the pipeline (fmask cache read latency hiding fifo) is full and stalling the fmask cache so the cache cannot output any transactions. " = 0x59, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_STALL: Number of cycles the fmask cache is stalled. This is the combined cache stall signal. " = 0x5a, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_FLUSH: This is the number of fmask cache flushes. " = 0x5b, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_TAGS_FLUSHED: Number of dirty tags that are flushed (the fmask cache has 64 tags). " = 0x5c, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_SECTORS_FLUSHED: Number of valid sectors (i.e they have valid data) per dirty tags that are flushed (the fmask cache has 4 sectors per tag). The valid sectors may be dirty. The total valid non-dirty sectors in flushed out tags = CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_SECTORS_FLUSHED - CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_DIRTY_SECTORS_FLUSHED. " = 0x5d, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_DIRTY_SECTORS_FLUSHED: Number of dirty sectors per dirty tags that are flushed (the fmask cache has 4 sectors per tag). " = 0x5e, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_HIT: Number of quad fragment transactions that hit the color cache (TAG HIT && SECTOR HIT). It is a hit if you hit the tag and a sector in that tag meaning that sector's data is valid.
Total probe transactions = quads in CB_PERF_SEL_CC_IB_TB_FRAG_VALID_READY = CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_HIT+CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS " = 0x5f, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_TAG_MISS: Number of quad fragment transactions that have color cache tag misses  (TAG MISS).  A tag miss is when there isn't a tag that matches the input.  Because of sectoring, a tag hit does not imply that the required data is in the cache (i.e TAG HIT && SECTOR MISS). " = 0x60, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS: Number of quad fragment transactions that have color cache sector miss (TAG MISS || SECTOR MISS).  A sector miss is when the required sector is not in the cache.  Tag misses are included in this count because a sector cannot be in the cache if there is no tag for it.
 Total transactions that have TAG HIT && SECTOR MISS = CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS - CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_TAG_MISS. " = 0x61, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_REEVICTION_STALL: Number of cycles the color cache is stalled because it is trying to evict a line that already has a pending evict. This can happen when a cacheline has been written out to memory and waiting for the write ack gets a hit again, eventually becoming dirty and needing to be re-evicted. Since only one eviction per cacheline can be outstanding, the cache is stalled. " = 0x62, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_EVICT_NONZERO_INFLIGHT_STALL: Number of cycles the color cache is stalled because it is trying to evict a line that has a nonzero inflight count.
When a cachelines LRU count reaches the scaled eviction point set by CC_CACHE_EVICT_POINT and it is still inflight then this counter get incremented
This is usually a sign that the cache is unable to withstand the memory read latency. CC_CACHE_EVICT_POINT can be set to a LOWER value to handle the increased read latency. " = 0x63, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_REPLACE_PENDING_EVICT_STALL: Number of cycles the color cache is stalled because the line being replaced has a pending evict. This happens when the cacheline chosen for allocation on a miss is still waiting for its write-ack to return from a previous eviction. This is usually a sign that the cache is unable to withstand the memory write latency. CC_CACHE_EVICT_POINT can be set to a HIGHER value to handle the increased write latency. " = 0x64, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_INFLIGHT_COUNTER_MAXIMUM_STALL: Number of cycles the color cache is stalled because one of the inflight counters has reached the maximum value. " = 0x65, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_READ_OUTPUT_STALL: Number of cycles the color cache is stalled because the read request output path is stalled. This can happen due to increased memory read request ask-go latency " = 0x66, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_WRITE_OUTPUT_STALL: Number of cycles the color cache is stalled because the write request output path is stalled. This can happen due to increased memory write request ask-go latency " = 0x67, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_ACK_OUTPUT_STALL: Number of cycles the color cache is stalled because the acknowledge output path is stalled. This can happen if the next stage in the pipeline (color cache read latency hiding fifo) is full and stalling the color cache so the cache cannot output any transactions. " = 0x68, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_STALL: Number of cycles the color cache is stalled. This is the combined cache stall signal. " = 0x69, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_FLUSH: This is the number of color cache flushes.  This is includes surface sync flushes. " = 0x6a, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_TAGS_FLUSHED: Number of dirty tags that are flushed (the color cache has 64 tags). " = 0x6b, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_SECTORS_FLUSHED: Number of valid sectors (i.e they have valid data) per dirty tags that are flushed (the color cache has 4 sectors per tag). The valid sectors may be dirty. The total valid non-dirty sectors in flushed out tags = CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_SECTORS_FLUSHED - CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_DIRTY_SECTORS_FLUSHED. " = 0x6c, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_DIRTY_SECTORS_FLUSHED: Number of dirty sectors per dirty tags that are flushed (the color cache has 4 sectors per tag). " = 0x6d, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_WA_TO_RMW_CONVERSION: The number of color cache probe transactions that hit a write allocate cache line that convert it into a read-modify-write cache line because they need destination buffer data. " = 0x6e, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_READS_SAVED_DUE_TO_DCC: Number of reads prevented by DCC. " = 0x6f, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CB_TAP_WRREQ_VALID_READY: Number of cycles the CB to TAP write request interface is valid and ready.  This is measured at the interface converter rather than directly on the interface. The should be equal to the sum of CB_PERF_SEL_*_MC_WRITE_REQUEST " = 0x70, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CB_TAP_WRREQ_VALID_READYB: Number of cycles the CB to TAP write request interface is valid and not ready.  This is measured at the interface converter rather than directly on the interface. " = 0x71, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CB_TAP_WRREQ_VALIDB_READY: Number of cycles the CB to TAP write request interface is valid and ready.  This is measured at the interface converter rather than directly on the interface. " = 0x72, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CB_TAP_WRREQ_VALIDB_READYB: Number of cycles the CB to TAP write request interface is not valid and not ready.  This is measured at the interface converter rather than directly on the interface. " = 0x73, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_MC_WRITE_REQUEST: Number of 32-byte cmask mc write requests. " = 0x74, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_MC_WRITE_REQUEST: Number of 32-byte fmask mc write requests. " = 0x75, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_MC_WRITE_REQUEST: Number of 32-byte color mc write requests. " = 0x76, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_MC_WRITE_REQUESTS_IN_FLIGHT: Number of 32-byte cmask mc write requests in flight.  CB_PERF_SEL_CM_MC_WRITE_REQUESTS_IN_FLIGHT/CB_PERF_SEL_CM_MC_WRITE_REQUEST = average latency. " = 0x77, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_MC_WRITE_REQUESTS_IN_FLIGHT: Number of 32-byte fmask mc write requests in flight.  CB_PERF_SEL_FC_MC_WRITE_REQUESTS_IN_FLIGHT/CB_PERF_SEL_FC_MC_WRITE_REQUEST = average latency. " = 0x78, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_MC_WRITE_REQUESTS_IN_FLIGHT: Number of 32-byte color mc write requests in flight.  CB_PERF_SEL_CC_MC_WRITE_REQUESTS_IN_FLIGHT/CB_PERF_SEL_CC_MC_WRITE_REQUEST = average latency. " = 0x79, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CB_TAP_RDREQ_VALID_READY: Number of cycles the CB to TAP read request interface is valid and ready.  This is measured at the interface converter rather than directly on the interface. " = 0x7a, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CB_TAP_RDREQ_VALID_READYB: Number of cycles the CB to TAP read request interface is valid and not ready.  This is measured at the interface converter rather than directly on the interface. " = 0x7b, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CB_TAP_RDREQ_VALIDB_READY: Number of cycles the CB to TAP read request interface is not valid and ready.  This is measured at the interface converter rather than directly on the interface. " = 0x7c, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CB_TAP_RDREQ_VALIDB_READYB: Number of cycles the CB to TAP read request interface is not valid and not ready.  This is measured at the interface converter rather than directly on the interface. " = 0x7d, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_MC_READ_REQUEST: Number of 32-byte cmask mc read requests.  Cmask does not make 32-byte requests, so the counter will report the equivalent number of 32-byte requests. " = 0x7e, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_MC_READ_REQUEST: Number of 32-byte fmask mc read requests. " = 0x7f, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_MC_READ_REQUEST: Number of 32-byte color mc read requests.  Color does not make 32-byte requests, so the counter will report the equivalent number of 32-byte requests. " = 0x80, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_MC_READ_REQUESTS_IN_FLIGHT: Number of 32-byte cmask mc read requests in flight.  Cmask does not make 32-byte requests, so the counter will report the equivalent number of 32-byte requests.  CB_PERF_SEL_CM_MC_READ_REQUESTS_IN_FLIGHT/CB_PERF_SEL_CM_MC_READ_REQUEST = average latency. " = 0x81, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_MC_READ_REQUESTS_IN_FLIGHT: Number of 32-byte fmask mc read requests in flight.  CB_PERF_SEL_FC_MC_READ_REQUESTS_IN_FLIGHT/CB_PERF_SEL_FC_MC_READ_REQUEST = average latency. " = 0x82, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_MC_READ_REQUESTS_IN_FLIGHT: Number of 32-byte color mc read requests in flight.  Color does not make 32-byte requests, so the counter will report the equivalent number of 32-byte requests.  CB_PERF_SEL_CC_MC_READ_REQUESTS_IN_FLIGHT/CB_PERF_SEL_CC_MC_READ_REQUEST = average latency. " = 0x83, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_TQ_FULL: Number of cycles the cmask tile queue is full. This fifo covers the cmask memory read latency and stalling indicates that this fifo does not have enough latency hiding capacity " = 0x84, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_TQ_FIFO_TILE_RESIDENCY_STALL: Number of cycles the cmask read latency hiding fifo's head entry is waiting for cmask read data to return from memory and become resident in cache so the transaction can be popped. This does not mean that cmask logic is stalled, look at CB_PERF_SEL_CM_TQ_FULL for that. " = 0x85, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_QUAD_RDLAT_FIFO_FULL: Number of cycles the fmask read latency quad fifo is full. This fifo covers the fmask memory read latency and stalling indicates that this fifo does not have enough latency hiding capacity " = 0x86, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_TILE_RDLAT_FIFO_FULL: Number of cycles the fmask read latency tile fifo is full. This fifo covers the fmask memory read latency and stalling indicates that this fifo does not have enough latency hiding capacity " = 0x87, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_RDLAT_FIFO_QUAD_RESIDENCY_STALL: Number of cycles the fmask read latency hiding fifo's head entry is waiting for fmask read data to return from memory and become resident in cache so the transaction can be popped. This does not mean that fmask logic is stalled, look at CB_PERF_SEL_FC_QUAD_RDLAT_FIFO_FULL || CB_PERF_SEL_FC_TILE_RDLAT_FIFO_FULL for that.  " = 0x88, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FOP_FMASK_RAW_STALL: Number of cycles a quadA-quadA sequence (back-to-back) is stalled because of a read-after-write conflict in fragop block. " = 0x89, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FOP_FMASK_BYPASS_STALL: Number of cycles a quadA-quadB-quadA sequence is stalled because of a read-after-write conflict in fragop block. " = 0x8a, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_SF_FULL: Number of cycles the color cache source fifo is full. This fifo covers the fmask memory read plus color cache memory read latency and stalling indicates that this fifo does not have enough latency hiding capacity " = 0x8b, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_FULL: Number of cycles the color cache reorder buffer is full. This fifo covers the color cache memory read latency and stalling indicates that this fifo does not have enough latency hiding capacity " = 0x8c, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_EVENFIFO_QUAD_RESIDENCY_STALL: Number of cycles the color even side read latency hiding fifo's head entry is waiting for even 32B color read data to return from memory and become resident in cache so the transaction can be popped. This does not mean that color logic is stalled, look at CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_FULL for that. " = 0x8d, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_ODDFIFO_QUAD_RESIDENCY_STALL: Number of cycles the color odd side read latency hiding fifo's head entry is waiting for odd 32B color read data to return from memory and become resident in cache so the transaction can be popped. This does not mean that color logic is stalled, look at CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_FULL for that. " = 0x8e, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_BLENDER_RAW_HAZARD_STALL: Number of cycles the blend pipeline is stalled to handle read after write hazards. " = 0x8f, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_EVENT: Total number of events reaching the CB.  This includes events that the CB does not process. " = 0x90, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_EVENT_CACHE_FLUSH_TS: Number of CACHE_FLUSH_TS events " = 0x91, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_EVENT_CONTEXT_DONE: Number of CONTEXT_DONE  events " = 0x92, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_EVENT_CACHE_FLUSH: Number of CACHE_FLUSH events " = 0x93, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_EVENT_CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INV_TS_EVENT: Number of CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INV_TS_EVENT events " = 0x94, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_EVENT_CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INV_EVENT: Number of_CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INV_EVENTevents " = 0x95, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_EVENT_FLUSH_AND_INV_CB_DATA_TS: Number of FLUSH_AND_INV_CB_DATA_TS events " = 0x96, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_EVENT_FLUSH_AND_INV_CB_META: Number of FLUSH_AND_INV_CB_META events " = 0x97, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_SURFACE_SYNC: Number of surface syncs " = 0x98, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CMASK_READ_DATA_0xC: Number of fmask cache probe misses that read cmask with a value of 0xC. A value of 0xC means that a fmask tile requires 0 bit planes. Sum of CB_PERF_SEL_CMASK_READ_DATA_* should match CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS. " = 0x99, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CMASK_READ_DATA_0xD: Number of fmask cache probe misses that read cmask with a value of 0xD. A value of 0xD means that a fmask tile requires 1 bit planes. Sum of CB_PERF_SEL_CMASK_READ_DATA_* should match CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS. " = 0x9a, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CMASK_READ_DATA_0xE: Number of fmask cache probe misses that read cmask with a value of 0xE. A value of 0xE means that a fmask tile requires 2 bit planes. Sum of CB_PERF_SEL_CMASK_READ_DATA_* should match CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS. " = 0x9b, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CMASK_READ_DATA_0xF: Number of fmask cache probe misses that read cmask with a value of 0xF. A value of 0xF means that a fmask tile requires 3 bit planes. Sum of CB_PERF_SEL_CMASK_READ_DATA_* should match CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS. " = 0x9c, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CMASK_WRITE_DATA_0xC: Number of tiles that wrote a value of 0xC to cmask.  Cmask writes occur at the end of a tile.  The hardware does not perform the write if fmask has not changed, but the counter will update as if regardless of whether the hardware wrote or not. A value of 0xC means that a fmask tile requires 0 bit planes. Sum of all CB_PERF_SEL_CMASK_WRITE_DATA_* equals cmask cache probes (CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_HIT + CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS). " = 0x9d, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CMASK_WRITE_DATA_0xD: Number of tile that wrote a value of 0xD was written to cmask.  Cmask writes occur at the end of a tile.  The hardware does not perform the write if fmask has not changed, but the counter will update as if regardless of whether the hardware wrote or not. A value of 0xD means that a fmask tile requires 1 bit planes. Sum of all CB_PERF_SEL_CMASK_WRITE_DATA_* equals cmask cache probes (CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_HIT + CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS). " = 0x9e, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CMASK_WRITE_DATA_0xE: Number of tiles that wrote a value of 0xE was written to cmask.  Cmask writes occur at the end of a tile.  The hardware does not perform the write if fmask has not changed, but the counter will update as if regardless of whether the hardware wrote or not. A value of 0xE means that a fmask tile requires 2 bit planes. Sum of all CB_PERF_SEL_CMASK_WRITE_DATA_* equals cmask cache probes (CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_HIT + CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS). " = 0x9f, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CMASK_WRITE_DATA_0xF: Number of tiles that wrote a value of 0xF was written to cmask.  Cmask writes occur at the end of a tile.  The hardware does not perform the write if fmask has not changed, but the counter will update as if regardless of whether the hardware wrote or not. A value of 0xF means that a fmask tile requires 3 bit planes. Sum of all CB_PERF_SEL_CMASK_WRITE_DATA_* equals cmask cache probes (CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_HIT + CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS). " = 0xa0, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_TWO_PROBE_QUAD_FRAGMENT: Number of quad fragments that require two cache probes.  AA blending can create these when the read fragment does not match the write fragment. " = 0xa1, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_EXPORT_32_ABGR_QUAD_FRAGMENT: Number of EXPORT_32_ABGR quad fragments.  It takes two clocks to send the src color data for these. " = 0xa2, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_DUAL_SOURCE_COLOR_QUAD_FRAGMENT: Number of dual source blending color quad fragments " = 0xa3, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_HAS_1_FRAGMENT_BEFORE_UPDATE: Number of quads that started with 1 fragment in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xa4, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_HAS_2_FRAGMENTS_BEFORE_UPDATE: Number of quads that started with 2 fragments in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xa5, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_HAS_3_FRAGMENTS_BEFORE_UPDATE: Number of quads that started with 3 fragments in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xa6, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_HAS_4_FRAGMENTS_BEFORE_UPDATE: Number of quads that started with 4 fragments in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xa7, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_HAS_5_FRAGMENTS_BEFORE_UPDATE: Number of quads that started with 5 fragments in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xa8, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_HAS_6_FRAGMENTS_BEFORE_UPDATE: Number of quads that started with 6 fragments in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xa9, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_HAS_7_FRAGMENTS_BEFORE_UPDATE: Number of quads that started with 7 fragments in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xaa, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_HAS_8_FRAGMENTS_BEFORE_UPDATE: Number of quads that started with 8 fragments in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xab, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_HAS_1_FRAGMENT_AFTER_UPDATE: Number of quads that ended up with 1 fragment in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xac, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_HAS_2_FRAGMENTS_AFTER_UPDATE: Number of quads that ended up with 2 fragments in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xad, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_HAS_3_FRAGMENTS_AFTER_UPDATE: Number of quads that ended up with 3 fragments in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xae, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_HAS_4_FRAGMENTS_AFTER_UPDATE: Number of quads that ended up with 4 fragments in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xaf, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_HAS_5_FRAGMENTS_AFTER_UPDATE: Number of quads that ended up with 5 fragments in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xb0, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_HAS_6_FRAGMENTS_AFTER_UPDATE: Number of quads that ended up with 6 fragments in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xb1, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_HAS_7_FRAGMENTS_AFTER_UPDATE: Number of quads that ended up with 7 fragments in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xb2, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_HAS_8_FRAGMENTS_AFTER_UPDATE: Number of quads that ended up with 8 fragments in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xb3, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_ADDED_1_FRAGMENT: Number of quads that added 1 fragment in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xb4, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_ADDED_2_FRAGMENTS: Number of quads that added 2 fragments in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xb5, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_ADDED_3_FRAGMENTS: Number of quads that added 3 fragments in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xb6, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_ADDED_4_FRAGMENTS: Number of quads that added 4 fragments in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xb7, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_ADDED_5_FRAGMENTS: Number of quads that added 5 fragments in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xb8, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_ADDED_6_FRAGMENTS: Number of quads that added 6 fragments in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xb9, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_ADDED_7_FRAGMENTS: Number of quads that added 7 fragments in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xba, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_REMOVED_1_FRAGMENT: Number of quads that removed 1 fragment in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xbb, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_REMOVED_2_FRAGMENTS: Number of quads that removed 2 fragments in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xbc, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_REMOVED_3_FRAGMENTS: Number of quads that removed 3 fragments in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xbd, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_REMOVED_4_FRAGMENTS: Number of quads that removed 4 fragments in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xbe, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_REMOVED_5_FRAGMENTS: Number of quads that removed 5 fragments in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xbf, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_REMOVED_6_FRAGMENTS: Number of quads that removed 6 fragments in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xc0, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_REMOVED_7_FRAGMENTS: Number of quads that removed 7 fragments in AA mode in fragop block. " = 0xc1, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_READS_FRAGMENT_0: Number of quads that reads fragment 0 to the color cache. " = 0xc2, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_READS_FRAGMENT_1: Number of quads that reads fragment 1 to the color cache. " = 0xc3, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_READS_FRAGMENT_2: Number of quads that reads fragment 2 to the color cache. " = 0xc4, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_READS_FRAGMENT_3: Number of quads that reads fragment 3 to the color cache. " = 0xc5, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_READS_FRAGMENT_4: Number of quads that reads fragment 4 to the color cache. " = 0xc6, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_READS_FRAGMENT_5: Number of quads that reads fragment 5 to the color cache. " = 0xc7, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_READS_FRAGMENT_6: Number of quads that reads fragment 6 to the color cache. " = 0xc8, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_READS_FRAGMENT_7: Number of quads that reads fragment 7 to the color cache. " = 0xc9, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_WRITES_FRAGMENT_0: Number of quads that writes fragment 0 to the color cache. " = 0xca, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_WRITES_FRAGMENT_1: Number of quads that writes fragment 1 to the color cache. " = 0xcb, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_WRITES_FRAGMENT_2: Number of quads that writes fragment 2 to the color cache. " = 0xcc, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_WRITES_FRAGMENT_3: Number of quads that writes fragment 3 to the color cache. " = 0xcd, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_WRITES_FRAGMENT_4: Number of quads that writes fragment 4 to the color cache. " = 0xce, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_WRITES_FRAGMENT_5: Number of quads that writes fragment 5 to the color cache. " = 0xcf, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_WRITES_FRAGMENT_6: Number of quads that writes fragment 6 to the color cache. " = 0xd0, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_WRITES_FRAGMENT_7: Number of quads that writes fragment 7 to the color cache. " = 0xd1, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_BLEND_OPT_DONT_READ_DST: Number of quads that were blending but enabled optimization to not need read destination data. This optimization can be disabled by setting DISABLE_BLEND_OPT_DONT_RD_DST. " = 0xd2, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_BLEND_OPT_BLEND_BYPASS: Number of quads that were blending but enabled optimization to bypassed blend operation. This optimization can be disabled by setting DISABLE_BLEND_OPT_BYPASS. " = 0xd3, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_BLEND_OPT_DISCARD_PIXELS: Number of quads that were blending but enabled optimization to discard at least 1 pixel. This optimization can be disabled by setting DISABLE_BLEND_OPT_DISCARD_PIXEL. " = 0xd4, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_DST_READ_COULD_HAVE_BEEN_OPTIMIZED: Number of quads that the blender detects that could have optimized away their destination reads (i.e destblend*dst == 0.0f).  NOTE:  this counter is not completely accurate and does not work for colors that have 32-bit components. " = 0xd5, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_BLENDING_COULD_HAVE_BEEN_BYPASSED: Number of quads that the blender detects that could have optimized away blending (destblend*dst == 0.0f && srcblend*src == 1.0f).  NOTE:  this counter is not completely accurate and does not work for colors that have 32-bit components. " = 0xd6, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_COULD_HAVE_BEEN_DISCARDED: Number of quads that the blender detects that could have discarded some pixels (destblend*dst == 1.0f && srcblend*src == 0.0f).  NOTE:  this counter is not completely accurate and does not work for colors that have 32-bit components. " = 0xd7, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_BLEND_OPT_PIXELS_RESULT_EQ_DEST: Number of blended pixels that the blender detects can be dropped because the blended result is the same as the original destination value. " = 0xd8, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_DRAWN_BUSY: Number of busy cycles around the stage calculating the CB_PERF_SEL_DRAWN_* counters. Used as denominator for all the CB_PERF_SEL_DRAWN_* counters.  Filtering using CB_PERFCOUNTER_FILTER fields has an effect in this mode. " = 0xd9, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_TILE_TO_CMR_REGION_BUSY: Number of busy cycles b/w PERFCOUNTER_START and PERFCOUNTER_STOP for the pipeline region b/w DB_CB_TILE and CMASK CACHE READ.
 This can be used as denominator for rate calculation for counters in this region
 " = 0xda, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CMR_TO_FCR_REGION_BUSY: Number of busy cycles b/w PERFCOUNTER_START and PERFCOUNTER_STOP for the pipeline region b/w CMASK CACHE READ and FMASK CACHE READ.
 This can be used as denominator for rate calculation for counters in this region
 " = 0xdb, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FCR_TO_CCR_REGION_BUSY: Number of busy cycles b/w PERFCOUNTER_START and PERFCOUNTER_STOP for the pipeline region b/w FMASK CACHE READ and COLOR CACHE READ.
 This can be used as denominator for rate calculation for counters in this region
 " = 0xdc, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CCR_TO_CCW_REGION_BUSY: Number of busy cycles b/w PERFCOUNTER_START and PERFCOUNTER_STOP for the pipeline region b/w COLOR CACHE READ and COLOR CACHE WRITE.
 This can be used as denominator for rate calculation for counters in this region
 " = 0xdd, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_PF_SLOW_MODE_QUAD_EMPTY_HALF_DROPPED: Number of lquad transactions (halves of slow mode 2-cycle quad) that were dropped in fc_merge logic due to optimization from going into the SRC fifo because the pixel pair in that half quad was unlit.
 This optimization can be disabled by setting: DISABLE_SLOW_MODE_EMPTY_HALF_QUAD_KILL
 " = 0xde, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_SEQUENCER_CLEAR: Number of quads that are generated to expand out the fast clear color as well as number of drawn quads that have partially lit pixels so that unlit samples need to expands their fast clear color.
Use CB_PERF_SEL_DRAWN_BUSY as denominator to get per clock rates.
 " = 0xdf, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_SEQUENCER_ELIMINATE_FAST_CLEAR: Number of quads generated during ELIMINATE_FAST_CLEAR pass to expand their fast clear color
Use CB_PERF_SEL_DRAWN_BUSY as denominator to get per clock rates.
 " = 0xe0, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_SEQUENCER_FMASK_DECOMPRESS: Number of quads generated during FMASK_DECOMPRESS pass to expand their fast clear color
Use CB_PERF_SEL_DRAWN_BUSY as denominator to get per clock rates.
 " = 0xe1, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_SEQUENCER_FMASK_COMPRESSION_DISABLE: Number of quad fragments seen during normal rendering when the state was set to disable fmask compression. This will include drawn quads as well as generated quads to expand their fast clear
Use CB_PERF_SEL_DRAWN_BUSY as denominator to get per clock rates.
 " = 0xe2, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_KEYID_RDLAT_FIFO_FULL: Number of cycles the fmask read latency keyid fifo is full. This fifo covers the fmask memory read latency and stalling indicates that this fifo does not have enough latency hiding capacity " = 0xe3, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DOC_IS_STALLED: Number of cycles the overwrite combiner is stalled. " = 0xe4, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DOC_MRTS_NOT_COMBINED: Number of times a quad's mrt was not able to be combined with another one (so as to share the same quarter-tile cam entry). " = 0xe5, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DOC_MRTS_COMBINED: Number of times a quad's mrt was combined with another one (so as to share the same quarter-tile cam entry). " = 0xe6, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DOC_QTILE_CAM_MISS: Number of misses in the overwrite combiner's quarter-tile cam. " = 0xe7, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DOC_QTILE_CAM_HIT: Number of hits in the overwrite combiner's quarter-tile cam. " = 0xe8, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DOC_CLINE_CAM_MISS: Number of misses in the overwrite combiner's cacheline cam. " = 0xe9, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DOC_CLINE_CAM_HIT: Number of hits in the overwrite combiner's cacheline cam. " = 0xea, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DOC_QUAD_PTR_FIFO_IS_FULL: Number of cycles that the overwrite combiner's quad pointer fifo is full. " = 0xeb, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DOC_OVERWROTE_1_SECTOR: Number of times that the overwrite combiner overwrote just 1 sector. " = 0xec, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DOC_OVERWROTE_2_SECTORS: Number of times that the overwrite combiner overwrote just 2 sector. " = 0xed, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DOC_OVERWROTE_3_SECTORS: Number of times that the overwrite combiner overwrote just 3 sector. " = 0xee, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DOC_OVERWROTE_4_SECTORS: Number of times that the overwrite combiner overwrote all 4 sectors. " = 0xef, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DOC_TOTAL_OVERWRITTEN_SECTORS: Number of total sectors overwritten by the Overwrite Combiner. " = 0xf0, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DCC_CACHE_HIT: Number of hits in the DCC cache (TAG HIT && SECTOR HIT). " = 0xf1, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DCC_CACHE_TAG_MISS: Number of tag misses in the DCC cache (TAG MISS). " = 0xf2, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DCC_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS: Number of sector misses in the DCC cache (TAG MISS || SECTOR MISS). " = 0xf3, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DCC_CACHE_REEVICTION_STALL: Number of cycles the DCC cache is stalled because it is trying to evict a line that already has a pending evict. This can happen when a cacheline has been written out to memory and waiting for the write ack gets a hit again, eventually becoming dirty and needing to be re-evicted. Since only one eviction per cacheline can be outstanding, the cache is stalled. " = 0xf4, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DCC_CACHE_EVICT_NONZERO_INFLIGHT_STALL: Number of cycles the DCC cache is stalled because it is trying to evict a line that has a nonzero inflight count.
When a cachelines LRU count reaches the scaled eviction point set by DCC_CACHE_EVICT_POINT and it is still inflight then this counter get incremented
This is usually a sign that the cache is unable to withstand the memory read latency. DCC_CACHE_EVICT_POINT can be set to a LOWER value to handle the increased read latency.
This count is the number of times the Key Cache sends a panic to the Color Cache. " = 0xf5, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DCC_CACHE_REPLACE_PENDING_EVICT_STALL: Number of cycles the DCC cache is stalled because the line being replaced has a pending evict. This happens when the cacheline chosen for allocation on a miss is still waiting for its write-ack to return from a previous eviction. This is usually a sign that the cache is unable to withstand the memory write latency. DCC_CACHE_EVICT_POINT can be set to a HIGHER value to handle the increased write latency. " = 0xf6, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DCC_CACHE_INFLIGHT_COUNTER_MAXIMUM_STALL: Number of cycles the DCC cache is stalled because one of the inflight counters has reached the maximum value. " = 0xf7, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DCC_CACHE_READ_OUTPUT_STALL: Number of cycles the DCC cache is stalled because the read request output path is stalled. This can happen due to increased memory read request ask-go latency " = 0xf8, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DCC_CACHE_WRITE_OUTPUT_STALL: Number of cycles the DCC cache is stalled because the write request output path is stalled. This can happen due to increased memory write request ask-go latency " = 0xf9, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DCC_CACHE_ACK_OUTPUT_STALL: Number of cycles the DCC cache is stalled because the acknowledge output path is stalled. This can happen if the next stage in the pipeline (DCC cache read latency hiding fifo) is full and stalling the DCC cache so the cache cannot output any transactions. " = 0xfa, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DCC_CACHE_STALL: Number of cycles the DCC cache is stalled. This is the combined cache stall signal. " = 0xfb, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DCC_CACHE_FLUSH: This is the number of DCC cache flushes. " = 0xfc, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DCC_CACHE_TAGS_FLUSHED: Number of dirty tags that are flushed (the DCC cache has 32 tags). " = 0xfd, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DCC_CACHE_SECTORS_FLUSHED: Number of valid sectors (i.e they have valid data) per dirty tags that are flushed (the DCC cache has 1 sector per tag). The valid sectors may be dirty. The total valid non-dirty sectors in flushed out tags = CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DCC_CACHE_SECTORS_FLUSHED - CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DCC_CACHE_DIRTY_SECTORS_FLUSHED. " = 0xfe, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DCC_CACHE_DIRTY_SECTORS_FLUSHED: Number of dirty sectors per dirty tags that are flushed (the DCC cache has 1 sector per tag). " = 0xff, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_BEYOND_TILE_SPLIT: Number of fragments that lie outside the tile split boundary.  The color cache controller limits DCC compression support to only those fragments that are within the first tile split. " = 0x100, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_MC_DCC_WRITE_REQUEST: Number of 32-byte fmask mc DCC write requests. " = 0x101, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_MC_DCC_WRITE_REQUESTS_IN_FLIGHT: Number of 32-byte fmask mc DCC write requests in flight.  CB_PERF_SEL_FC_MC_DCC_WRITE_REQUESTS_IN_FLIGHT/CB_PERF_SEL_FC_MC_DCC_WRITE_REQUEST = average latency. " = 0x102, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_MC_DCC_READ_REQUEST: Number of 32-byte fmask mc DCC read requests. " = 0x103, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_MC_DCC_READ_REQUESTS_IN_FLIGHT: Number of 32-byte fmask mc DCC read requests in flight.  CB_PERF_SEL_FC_MC_DCC_READ_REQUESTS_IN_FLIGHT/CB_PERF_SEL_FC_MC_DCC_READ_REQUEST = average latency. " = 0x104, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_RDREQ_STALL: Number of times DCC read requests are stalled because the internal scoreboard predicts that the skid fifo will be full. " = 0x105, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_DECOMPRESS_TIDS_IN: Number of tids that come into the DCC's decompress module. " = 0x106, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_DECOMPRESS_TIDS_OUT: Number of tids that come out of the DCC's decompress module. " = 0x107, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_COMPRESS_TIDS_IN: Number of tids that come into the DCC's compress module. " = 0x108, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_COMPRESS_TIDS_OUT: Number of tids that come out of the DCC's compress module. " = 0x109, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_DCC_KEY_VALUE__CLEAR: From DCC cache:  Number of times all sectors of a cacheline were initialized with a register-defined clear value. " = 0x10a, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_KEY_VALUE__4_BLOCKS__2TO1: From DCC Compressor in Color Cache:  Number of times all 4 sectors were compressed as 2:1 blocks. " = 0x10b, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_KEY_VALUE__3BLOCKS_2TO1__1BLOCK_2TO2: From DCC Compressor in Color Cache:  Number of times sectors 1 through 3 were compressed as 2:1 blocks and sector 0 was compressed as 2:2 (uncompressed). " = 0x10c, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_KEY_VALUE__2BLOCKS_2TO1__1BLOCK_2TO2__1BLOCK_2TO1: From DCC Compressor in Color Cache:  Number of times sectors 2 and 3 were compressed as 2:1 blocks, sector 1 was compressed as 2:2 (uncompressed) and sector 0 was compressed as 2:1 blocks. " = 0x10d, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_KEY_VALUE__1BLOCK_2TO1__1BLOCK_2TO2__2BLOCKS_2TO1: From DCC Compressor in Color Cache:  Number of times sector 3 was compressed as 2:1 blocks, sector 2 was compressed as 2:2 (uncompressed) and sectors 0 and 1 were compressed as 2:1 blocks. " = 0x10e, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_KEY_VALUE__1BLOCK_2TO2__3BLOCKS_2TO1: From DCC Compressor in Color Cache:  Number of times sector 3 was compressed as 2:2 (uncompressed) and sectors 0 through 2 were compressed as 2:1 blocks. " = 0x10f, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_KEY_VALUE__2BLOCKS_2TO1__2BLOCKS_2TO2: From DCC Compressor in Color Cache:  Number of times sectors 2 and 3 were compressed as 2:1 blocks and sectors 0 and 1 were compressed as 2:2 (uncompressed). " = 0x110, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_KEY_VALUE__1BLOCK_2TO1__2BLOCKS_2TO2__1BLOCK_2TO1: From DCC Compressor in Color Cache:  Number of times sector 3 was compressed as 2:1 blocks, sectors 1 and 2 were compressed as 2:2 (uncompressed) and sector 0 was compressed as 2:1 blocks. " = 0x111, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_KEY_VALUE__1BLOCK_2TO1__1BLOCK_2TO2__1BLOCK_2TO1__1BLOCK_2TO2: From DCC Compressor in Color Cache:  Number of times sector 3 was compressed as 2:1 blocks, sector 2 was compressed as 2:2 (uncompressed), sector 1 was compressed as 2:1 blocks and sector 0 was compressed as 2:2 (uncompressed). " = 0x112, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_KEY_VALUE__1BLOCK_2TO2__1BLOCK_2TO1__1BLOCK_2TO2__1BLOCK_2TO1: From DCC Compressor in Color Cache:  Number of times sector 3 was compressed as 2:2 (uncompressed), sector 2 was compressed as 2:1 blocks, sector 1 was compressed as 2:2 (uncompressed) and sector 0 was compressed as 2:1 blocks. " = 0x113, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_KEY_VALUE__2BLOCKS_2TO2__2BLOCKS_2TO1: From DCC Compressor in Color Cache:  Number of times sectors 2 and 3 were compressed as 2:2 (uncompressed) and sectors 0 and 1 were compressed as 2:1 blocks. " = 0x114, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_KEY_VALUE__1BLOCK_2TO2__2BLOCKS_2TO1__1BLOCK_2TO2: From DCC Compressor in Color Cache:  Number of times sector 3 was compressed as 2:2 (uncompressed), sectors 1 and 2 were compressed as 2:1 blocks and sector 0 was compressed as 2:2 (uncompressed). " = 0x115, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_KEY_VALUE__1BLOCK_2TO1__3BLOCKS_2TO2: From DCC Compressor in Color Cache:  Number of times sector 3 was compressed as 2:1 blocks and sectors 0 through 2 were compressed as 2:2 (uncompressed). " = 0x116, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_KEY_VALUE__1BLOCK_2TO2__1BLOCK_2TO1__2BLOCKS_2TO2: From DCC Compressor in Color Cache:  Number of times sector 3 was compressed as 2:2 (uncompressed), sector 2 was compressed as 2:1 blocks and sectors 0 and 1 were compressed as 2:2 (uncompressed). " = 0x117, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_KEY_VALUE__2BLOCKS_2TO2__1BLOCK_2TO1__1BLOCK_2TO2: From DCC Compressor in Color Cache:  Number of times sectors 2 and 3 were compressed as 2:2 (uncompressed), sector 1 was compressed as 2:1 blocks and sector 0 was compressed as 2:2 (uncompressed). " = 0x118, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_KEY_VALUE__3BLOCKS_2TO2__1BLOCK_2TO1: From DCC Compressor in Color Cache:  Number of times sectors 1 through 3 were compressed as 2:2 (uncompressed) and sector 0 was compressed as 2:1 blocks. " = 0x119, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_KEY_VALUE__2BLOCKS_4TO1: From DCC Compressor in Color Cache:  Number of times sectors 0 and 1 were compressed as 4:1 blocks. " = 0x11a, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_KEY_VALUE__1BLOCK_4TO1__1BLOCK_4TO2: From DCC Compressor in Color Cache:  Number of times sector 1 was compressed as 4:1 blocks and sector 0 was compressed as 4:2 blocks. " = 0x11b, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_KEY_VALUE__1BLOCK_4TO1__1BLOCK_4TO3: From DCC Compressor in Color Cache:  Number of times sector 1 was compressed as 4:1 blocks and sector 0 was compressed as 4:3 blocks. " = 0x11c, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_KEY_VALUE__1BLOCK_4TO1__1BLOCK_4TO4: From DCC Compressor in Color Cache:  Number of times sector 1 was compressed as 4:1 blocks and sector 0 was compressed as 4:4 (uncompressed). " = 0x11d, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_KEY_VALUE__1BLOCK_4TO2__1BLOCK_4TO1: From DCC Compressor in Color Cache:  Number of times sector 1 was compressed as 4:2 blocks and sector 0 was compressed as 4:1 blocks. " = 0x11e, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_KEY_VALUE__2BLOCKS_4TO2: From DCC Compressor in Color Cache:  Number of times sectors 0 and 1 were compressed as 4:2 blocks. " = 0x11f, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_KEY_VALUE__1BLOCK_4TO2__1BLOCK_4TO3: From DCC Compressor in Color Cache:  Number of times sector 1 was compressed as 4:2 blocks and sector 0 was compressed as 4:3 blocks. " = 0x120, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_KEY_VALUE__1BLOCK_4TO2__1BLOCK_4TO4: From DCC Compressor in Color Cache:  Number of times sector 1 was compressed as 4:2 blocks and sector 0 was compressed as 4:4 (uncompressed). " = 0x121, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_KEY_VALUE__1BLOCK_4TO3__1BLOCK_4TO1: From DCC Compressor in Color Cache:  Number of times sector 1 was compressed as 4:3 blocks and sector 0 was compressed as 4:1 blocks. " = 0x122, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_DCC_KEY_VALUE__1BLOCK_4TO3__1BLOCK_4TO2: From DCC Compressor in Color Cache:  Number of times sector 1 was compressed as 4:3 blocks and sector 0 was compressed as 4:2 blocks. " = 0x123, 
